{"name":"Cabbage","hex":"#87d7be","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cabbage","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An edible plant (Brassica oleracea var. capitata) having a head of green leaves.\n\n Any of various cultivars of the species Brassica oleracea.","Any of various cultivars of the species Brassica oleracea."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To form a head like that of the cabbage.","To do nothing; to idle; veg out."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cabbage"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cabbage","blocks":[{"text":"Cabbage, comprising several cultivars of Brassica oleracea, is a leafy green, red (purple), or white biennial plant grown as an annual vegetable crop for its dense-leaved heads. It is descended from the wild cabbage, and belongs to the \"cole crops\" or brassicas, meaning it is closely related to broccoli and cauliflower ; Brussels sprouts ; and Savoy cabbage."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Cabbage_and_cross_section_on_white.jpg/330px-Cabbage_and_cross_section_on_white.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cabbage","wikidata":"Q35051"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Brassica_oleracea_Helgoland1.jpg/500px-Brassica_oleracea_Helgoland1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Brassica_oleracea_Helgoland1.jpg/1280px-Brassica_oleracea_Helgoland1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Brassica_oleracea_Helgoland1.jpg/500px-Brassica_oleracea_Helgoland1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The cabbage inflorescence, which appears in the plant's second year of growth, features white or yellow flowers, each with four perpen